These files are courtesy of Unruly Lead Software Architect Shawn Wallace
They originate from a Raspberry Pi experiment for automated Splat testing.
The python scripts have a dependency on bluepy.btle, which, according to Shawn’s memory may have been Raspberry Pi-specific.
So this is not likely to run on a mac as-is.
The scripts center on controlling lights and sounds on splats.
opensplatScan.py returns BLE addresses of the Splats.
You need to plug in the address values found into the test code.

Files
opensplatlib.py
opensplatScan.py
opensplatTest.py
